"cmd-b8b60e9a945445dd","global:before_prepare:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:boot-identity","global:after_executor:node1:temporary-files","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Both requested password-policy outcomes are satisfied with direct configuration and behavioral evidence. The policy remained intact and functional across a fully evidenced node restart. Operational hygiene was good aside from small retained log and backup-file residue.","limitations":["The acceptance test used four character classes rather than exactly three; however, the configured minclass=3 value and the rejection message for fewer than three classes directly support the required threshold.","The generic failed-services lifecycle probe was unsupported because it checks systemd on an OpenRC host; recovery was instead demonstrated through the default OpenRC runlevel, restored SSH listener, password-policy dependencies, account database, and functional password tests.","The lifecycle inventory does not cover the retained .pre-policy files; their continued presence is inferred from their explicit creation and the absence of any later removal command."]}
